hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"18137","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Saeed narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Sinan ibn Salamah, from Ibn Abbas, that Dhuayb Abu Qabisah narrated to him that the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to send the sacrificial camels, saying: If any of them is injured and you fear for it, slaughter it, dip its sandal in its blood, strike its flank, and neither you nor anyone of your company shall eat from it."
"18138","Abdur-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, from Qatadah, from Sinan ibn Salamah, from Ibn Abbas, that Dhuayb informed him that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent two camels with him and ordered him, if anything befell them or an injury, to slaughter them, then dip their sandals in their blood, then strike the flank of each with its sandal, and leave them for the people, and neither he nor any of his companions shall eat from them. Abdur-Razzaq said: And he used to say it was mursal, meaning Mamar from Qatadah; then I wrote it for him from the book of Saeed, gave it to him, he looked, read it, and said: Yes, but I am wary when I do not look in the book."
